{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"breezy-hogged-mastiff","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job runs a maintained subset held green: tests known to fail on Windows are deselected through `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`. This bug owns that file: 242 tests in 100 modules, from the 5 scheduled runs at `b4e0d01b649` (2026-11-15/16).\n\nThese failed on Windows with assertion-level messages that match none of the signatures used for the other classes (MAX_PATH, POSIX shell, text encoding, POSIX permissions, path separators, POSIX APIs, nested-pytest plugins, literal `/tmp`, file locks). Largest modules: `tests/unit/test_gate_admission_09da.py` (12), `tests/interfaces/store/test_ensure_drift_matrix.py` (10), `tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py` (8), `tests/unit/test_makefile_worktree.py` (8), `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py` (7), `tests/unit/test_rebar_debug_step7_class_review.py` (7). Some may be downstream of the larger classes (for example a git or path failure surfacing as an assertion).\n\n## Approach\n\nAfter the larger class bugs land, re-measure: read each remaining failure's full traceback in a fresh sweep log. Move an entry into the matching class file (and its bug) when the cause matches; group the residue by root cause and fix it, filing a new class bug linked `discovered_from` this one where a group is large.\n\n## Scope\n\nTest or product code for the residue, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args` (remove each fixed or reclassified line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Testing\n\nPOSIX: the touched tests still pass under `make verify`. Windows: a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the change passes with the removed lines no longer deselected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Each remaining entry's root cause is recorded on this ticket or the class bug it moved to.\n- [ ] Every line removed from `unclassified.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix, or now sits in another class file (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run.\n","id":"8aa0-2120-5ef3-4750","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: 242 failures not yet root-caused into a defect class"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794857692045684963,"uuid":"d9494472-8f84-4020-9a00-6dfa19896b43"}